 switch keeps the player in the corner even while the card is visible. Audio file tracks keep playing while minimized and while the tab is in the background. A YouTube track only plays while its player is visible: when it is minimized, or when the desktop app's window is minimized or hidden in the tray, it pauses on that device only and resumes in sync with the room when it is shown again. Telsiz DJ gives the name of the playing track to your system's media controls and lock screen (Media Session), which can be turned off in the Media controls section of Settings > Privacy. Play and Pause there only affect that device. The bar of the player in the corner shows a pause on that device, and its Resume on This Device button resumes without affecting the room. The owner of the frequency can turn off Telsiz DJ or only the YouTube source.
